> Yacc/Bison input counts as a CFG, right?  

Only if there's no actual C code injected anywhere, and you're not
using tricks with error productions, which is how the current yacc
works.

If you can produce a yacc grammar with no auxilliary code, we would
be *VERY* happy indeed, but I'm nearly certain that elidable
terminators are not LR(1).  If they are possible as a CFG, they
almost certainly require LR(*) or LL(*), if not fully-general CFG
parsing; see http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_algorithms#Parsing
for some general CFG possibilities.

